<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie1bdacbfa58f19908f2c98dfbc91e469396239a1" commit="a8c097c2d5cf843989e94047bcf21bbf5a9bf411" commit_message="CRAS: dbus_control: Allow get/set hotword model via dbus  Similar to the cras_client interface, dbus method: GetNodes() returns a list of supported hotword models. SetHotwordModel() selects a hotword model.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48270 TEST=Verify Chrome HotwordService can get/set hotword models using CrasAudioHandler/CrasAudioClient with the added dbus messages. Verify Chrome receives the appropriate error code from SetHotwordModel dbus METHOD_RETURN when an invalid hotword model name is used.  Change-Id: Ie1bdacbfa58f19908f2c98dfbc91e469396239a1 Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388911 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388911" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/11/388911/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iabc4a6da31d90292ee0de48b54c19aac362bb434" commit="9e7f77a06ac4057884bdc4102e7699816f4dd25e" commit_message="CRAS: test_client: Show current hotword model name  Add a column in cras_test_client --dump_server_info to show the selected hotword model name on any hotword node.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48270 TEST=Verify the correct model name is displayed on Chell after cras_test_client --set_hotword_model 7:0:en_us cras_test_client --set_hotword_model 7:0:en_gb  Change-Id: Iabc4a6da31d90292ee0de48b54c19aac362bb434 Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388912 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388912" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/12/388912/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I23532d0b119c6c0b8a5c0965ac7c08a2399b08c6" commit="bfe943fae2ad453f6e0001f45a67369f011f5a16" commit_message="CRAS: Set a default hotword model on iodev init  If a hotword device supports the en_us locale, then set it as the default model during iodev init. This helps avoid breaking audio on SKL when the hotword device is opened before any model is set.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48270 TEST=Verify en_us is set after boot on Chell  Change-Id: I23532d0b119c6c0b8a5c0965ac7c08a2399b08c6 Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388913 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388913" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/13/388913/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4c8c0ae61a0e70c9fc211420bbf44bbc7d8de3ed" commit="a058a6691ee3abd39491941986943330c2e08418" commit_message="tpm: fix TPM reset  use the right prototype for the memset() clearing the TPM .bss space on reset, use addresses of variables instead of their values, and do not clear tpm_resisters.c .bss section, tpm_init() does the right thing.  BRANCH=gru BUG=chrome-os-partner:52366 TEST=make buildall  Change-Id: I4c8c0ae61a0e70c9fc211420bbf44bbc7d8de3ed Signed-off-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/389331 Commit-Ready: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="389331" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/31/389331/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I212166a23f9cd512d8f75315377d1f5620aea070" commit="c4adc8e82ae813bd9ccb86038267ef6c9771f731" commit_message="tpm: reset communications channels when resetting TPM  TPM resets happen asynchronously, conceivably there is some interface (i2cs or sps) activity under way when TPM is reset.  Sps driver provides a means of disconnecting the client of the driver, while the i2cs driver does not. Come to think of it, there is no real need to provide a special function to disconnect a client, this makes API simpler and allows to add driver initialization to the client registration function.  To make tpm_registers.c more flexible - allow to register a callback for interface initialization, this way when TPM is reset, the interface can be also re-initialized and is guaranteed to start from scratch after reset.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:52366 TEST=both firmware_TPMExtend and firmware_TPMKernelVersion autotests      pass  Change-Id: I212166a23f9cd512d8f75315377d1f5620aea070 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388886 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="388886" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/86/388886/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I947ed10f778009e189613e0588b765d19419b8cc" commit="74f59fa47533c6963e30240cf2f3552df7a2956d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: da7219: Reset codec gracefully, if still active  Currently the reset code in i2c_probe only resets the AAD part of the device and not the entire codec. This patch updates the driver to resolve this and ensures that if the codec is still active from a previous boot then the audio paths are powered down prior to reset.  Signed-off-by: Adam Thomson &lt;Adam.Thomson.Opensource@diasemi.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; Link: git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/broonie/sound.git tag: topic/da7219 (cherry picked from commit a7f16ea90ecffde4d4915eb7c81b11428e636920)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57840 TEST=Jack is detected when inserted in device's suspended state TEST=Jack removal is detected when removed in DUT's suspended state  Change-Id: I947ed10f778009e189613e0588b765d19419b8cc Signed-off-by: Sathyanarayana Nujella &lt;sathyanarayana.nujella@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/389633 Tested-by: Surendranath R Gurivireddy &lt;surendranath.r.gurivireddy@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="389633" owner_email="sathyanarayana.nujella@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/389633/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I113d8454716e77380f511387962f4bec42818b9e" commit="c7a32789c1ac63be05551b20281de3f1696b7e3f" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: da7219: Disable AAD if codec is not a wake-up source  Currently if AAD is enabled in the device, during system suspend the feature remains, regardless of whether the codec is a wake-up source or not. This means some additional power is being used which is unnecessary, and can causes issues with some platforms' IRQ handlers where state changes during system suspend aren't captured.  This patch updates the driver to disable AAD during suspend, if we're not a wake-up source, and then re-enables this on resume.  Signed-off-by: Adam Thomson &lt;Adam.Thomson.Opensource@diasemi.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; Link: git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/broonie/sound.git tag: topic/da7219 (cherry picked from commit bb0c35fcaf8f2ad3383dd43ca8abf5203cd06cc3)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57840 TEST=Jack is detected when inserted in device's suspended state TEST=Jack removal is detected when removed in DUT's suspended state  Change-Id: I113d8454716e77380f511387962f4bec42818b9e Signed-off-by: Sathyanarayana Nujella &lt;sathyanarayana.nujella@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/389634 Tested-by: Surendranath R Gurivireddy &lt;surendranath.r.gurivireddy@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="389634" owner_email="sathyanarayana.nujella@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/34/389634/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iea67463e6fcaba3383de84f39657663e9c25f622" commit="c858718b9cba0c970f5b0fe861ef86d98bd7fcca" commit_message="libcontainer: Allow users to specify mount() flags for rootfs  Since MS_BIND ignores all flags (except MS_REC) in favor of the original filesystem's flags, we need a second mount() call to set/remove any flags. This change adds methods to set/get such flags.  BUG=b:31630024 TEST=ARC still boots TEST=FEATURES=&quot;test&quot; emerge-${BOARD} chromeos-base/libcontainer  Change-Id: Iea67463e6fcaba3383de84f39657663e9c25f622 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388774 Commit-Ready: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388774" owner_email="lhchavez@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/74/388774/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7ac775fde9fbc8aa6c0caf5a31675762ba3de48a" commit="0396156f6deb66952fd60ecd134b3c58799be5a6" commit_message="login: Explicitly remount the container's rootfs with no flags  This change explicitly remounts the containers' rootfs with no flags, since it is mounted in Chrome OS with nosuid, noexec, nodev.  BUG=b:31630024 TEST=Android still boots. TEST=FEATURES=&quot;test&quot; emerge-${BOARD} chromeos-base/chromeos-login  Change-Id: I7ac775fde9fbc8aa6c0caf5a31675762ba3de48a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388775 Commit-Ready: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388775" owner_email="lhchavez@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/75/388775/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I58b8042e11654fcf2b6b15c356327dac5f64bef4" commit="0dd7a0f3594fd2f7dfeefb0483e8cb7c8dfe6ddc" commit_message="Adding av_webcam suite to run on av-flex DUT pool.  Over the last few weeks we've created a space in Cassandra to host some DUTs that the AV team can have better control over, regarding things like lighting and installation of custom test hardware. This change is intended to start making use of that pool for WebCam tests. Also, removing camera_perbuild because it is only being used by one test and is too generic for our use.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I58b8042e11654fcf2b6b15c356327dac5f64bef4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/387263 Commit-Ready: Vinayak Suley &lt;vsuley@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Rohit Makasana &lt;rohitbm@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vinayak Suley &lt;vsuley@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rohit Makasana &lt;rohitbm@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vinayak Suley &lt;vsuley@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="387263" owner_email="vsuley@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/63/387263/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If8b8c4f6123c9f53def0e115142a9781fd5f2575" commit="f64320d8e289cfcff0a6172ac2e4ce7da2aaaa36" commit_message="gru: disable wake_on_wifi  No other overlay has this enabled. Last I see, Wei-Ning said &quot;Wake on WiFi features are not complete yet.&quot; for oak.  This is causing major crashes on Kevin, since we're not waking up properly when the Wifi FW is trying to (e.g., with 'darkconnect').  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57054, chrome-os-partner:57527 TEST=don't see wake features configured with: dbus-send --print-reply --system --dest=org.chromium.flimflam /device/mlan0 org.chromium.flimflam.Device.GetProperties TEST=Step 7 shouldn't happen:   1. Boot to login screen   2. Connect to a Wifi AP   3. Enable 'darkconnect'. i.e.:   # dbus-send --print-reply --system --dest=org.chromium.flimflam /device/mlan0 org.chromium.flimflam.Device.SetProperty string:WakeOnWiFiFeaturesEnabled variant:string:&quot;darkconnect&quot;   4. Suspend for a while. e.g.:   # suspend_stress_test --count=1 --suspend_min=60 --suspend_max=90   5. Power off the AP (I just yanked the plug on my router)   6. Resume (RTC timer will kick off after about a minute)   7. Profit! No, actually you see &quot;Firmware wakeup failed&quot; and Wifi is thereafter dead  Change-Id: If8b8c4f6123c9f53def0e115142a9781fd5f2575 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Rev